{title: I Come with Joy to Meet My Lord}
{key: C}
{time: 6/8}

{start_of_verse: 1}
I [C]come with [F]joy to [G]meet my [C]Lord
For[C]given, [F]loved, and [G]free[**]
In [F]awe and [G]wonder [Em]to re[Am]call
His [Dm]life laid [**]down for [F]me[**], his [G]life laid [Dm]down for [C]me[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
I [C]come with [F]Christians [G]far and [C]near
To [C]find, as [F]all are [G]fed[**]
The [F]new com[G]muni[Em]ty of [Am]love
In [Dm]Christ's com[**]munion [F]bread[**], in [G]Christ's com[Dm]munion [C]bread[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
As [C]Christ breaks [F]bread and [G]bids us [C]share
Each [C]proud di[F]vision [G]ends[**]
The [F]love that [G]made us, [Em]makes us [Am]one
And [Dm]strangers [**]now are [F]friends[**], and [G]strangers [Dm]now are [C]friends[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
And [C]thus with [F]joy we [G]meet our [C]Lord
His [C]presence, [F]always [G]near[**]
Is [F]in such [G]friendship [Em]better [Am]known
We [Dm]see and [**]praise him [F]here[**], we [G]see and [Dm]praise him [C]here[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 5}
To[C]gether [F]met, to[G]gether [C]bound
We'll [C]go our [F]different [G]ways[**]
And [F]as his [G]people [Em]in the [Am]world
We'll [Dm]live and [**]speak his [F]praise[**], we'll [G]live and [Dm]speak his [C]praise[**].
{end_of_verse}
